  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): ASC 805 provides a measurement period of up to one year from the acquisition date during which the acquirer may adjust provisional amounts recognized in the purchase price allocation. Adjustments during this period are recorded retrospectively as if the accounting had been completed at the acquisition date.
Wrong (A): The measurement period is not unlimited; ASC 805 caps it at one year from the acquisition date.
Wrong (C): There is no six-month deadline in ASC 805; the standard allows up to twelve months.
Wrong (D): The measurement period runs from the acquisition date, not the fiscal year-end, so it may extend into a subsequent fiscal year.$EXPL$
