-- Q3148: Stock Compensation and Business Combinations [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 718-10-35-3, when forfeitures are recognized as they occur, the company reverses all previously recognized expense for forfeited awards. For 1,000 options at $5 fair value with 2 of 4 years vested, cumulative expense was 1,000 x $5 x (2/4) = $2,500, which is reversed in Year 2.
Wrong (B): When forfeitures occur under the as-they-occur method, an adjustment is required to reverse the expense previously recognized for those specific awards.
Wrong (C): Recognizing additional expense contradicts the forfeiture event; expense must be reversed, not increased.
Wrong (D): $1,250 would represent only one year of expense (1,000 x $5 x 1/4), but two years of cumulative expense must be reversed.$EXPL$
