-- Q3149: Stock Compensation and Business Combinations [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 805, assembled workforce does not meet the criteria for separate recognition as an identifiable intangible asset because it is generally not separable and does not arise from contractual or legal rights. Its value is therefore subsumed within goodwill.
Wrong (A): Assembled workforce fails the identifiability criterion (no contractual/legal right, not separable), so it cannot be recognized apart from goodwill.
Wrong (B): A workforce is not a tangible asset; it has no physical substance and does not belong in property, plant, and equipment.
Wrong (D): Assembled workforce is captured in goodwill as part of the purchase price allocation, not expensed in the acquisition period.$EXPL$
