-- Q3150: Stock Compensation and Business Combinations [easy/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 718, compensation expense for awards with only a service condition is recognized ratably over the requisite service period, which is typically the vesting period. The total expense equals the grant-date fair value of the awards expected to vest.
Wrong (A): Recognizing all expense at the grant date would front-load the cost and violate the matching principle; ASC 718 requires spreading expense over the service period.
Wrong (C): RSUs are not exercised like options; expense recognition is tied to the vesting period, not a future exercise event.
Wrong (D): The contractual life may exceed the vesting period; ASC 718 uses the requisite service period, not the contractual life, for recognition.$EXPL$
