-- Q3151: Stock Compensation and Business Combinations [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (D): A step acquisition occurs when an acquirer previously held a noncontrolling equity interest and subsequently acquires additional shares to obtain control. Under ASC 805, the previously held interest is remeasured to fair value at the acquisition date, with any resulting gain or loss recognized in earnings.
Wrong (A): Obtaining control in a single transaction is a standard business combination, not a step acquisition, because there is no previously held interest to remeasure.
Wrong (B): Selling a subsidiary to a third party is a disposal or deconsolidation event, not an acquisition.
Wrong (C): Pooling of interests was eliminated under SFAS 141 (now ASC 805); it is not a current method and does not describe a step acquisition.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3151;

-- Q3152: Stock Compensation and Business Combinations [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 805, in a step acquisition the previously held equity interest must be remeasured to acquisition-date fair value. The $3,000,000 gain ($15M fair value minus $12M carrying amount) is recognized in earnings in the period control is obtained.
Wrong (B): The remeasurement gain is recognized in earnings, not in other comprehensive income. ASC 805 requires income statement recognition for step acquisition adjustments.
Wrong (C): The acquirer cannot ignore the remeasurement; ASC 805 mandates fair value adjustment of the previously held interest at the acquisition date.
Wrong (D): A loss would only arise if fair value were below carrying amount; here fair value ($15M) exceeds the carrying amount ($12M), producing a gain.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3152;

