-- Q3155: Stock Compensation and Business Combinations [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 805, the acquirer in a business combination is the entity that obtains control of the other entity. Control is assessed by examining which entity transfers consideration, issues equity, or can elect the majority of the governing body.
Wrong (A): Larger revenue is an indicator considered when identifying the acquirer, but it is not determinative; control is the key criterion under ASC 805.
Wrong (C): Paying a higher price does not automatically make an entity the acquirer; the entity that obtains control is the acquirer regardless of price.
Wrong (D): Issuing the most shares may actually indicate the entity is the acquiree (a reverse acquisition), not the acquirer.$EXPL$
