  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 718, liability-classified awards such as cash-settled SARs are remeasured at fair value each reporting period, with changes in fair value recognized in compensation expense until the liability is settled. This differs from equity-classified awards, which are measured once at the grant date.
Wrong (A): Grant-date-only measurement applies to equity-classified awards; liability-classified awards require ongoing remeasurement each reporting period.
Wrong (B): Cash-settled SARs are settled in cash, not shares; settlement in shares would typically result in equity classification.
Wrong (D): Intrinsic value measurement at grant date only is not the required approach; ASC 718 requires fair value remeasurement each period for liability awards.$EXPL$
