-- Q3164: Advanced Consolidations [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 810-10-45-1, the subsidiary''s equity accounts (common stock, APIC, and retained earnings) are eliminated against the parent''s investment in subsidiary account in the consolidation entry. This prevents double-counting because the parent''s investment balance already represents its share of the subsidiary''s net assets.
Wrong (A): Adding subsidiary equity to the parent''s equity would double-count net assets already represented by the parent''s investment balance.
Wrong (C): Reporting subsidiary equity separately would misrepresent the consolidated entity as having two distinct equity pools rather than one unified equity structure.
Wrong (D): Subsidiary equity accounts represent ownership interests, not obligations; reclassifying them as liabilities has no basis under GAAP.$EXPL$
