-- Q3178: Advanced Consolidations [medium/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under ASC 810, intercompany sales are eliminated in consolidation and the land is reported at its original book value to the consolidated entity of $200,000. The $100,000 intercompany gain is removed because no transaction occurred with an outside party.
Wrong (A): $300,000 is the intercompany transfer price, which reflects an internal transaction that must be eliminated; the consolidated entity reports the land at its original cost.
Wrong (B): $250,000 has no basis in the facts; neither partial elimination nor averaging is appropriate for intercompany asset transfers.
Wrong (D): $100,000 represents the intercompany gain, not the land''s reportable value; the land must be carried at its pre-transfer book value of $200,000.$EXPL$
