-- Q3180: Advanced Consolidations [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): In a downstream sale (parent to subsidiary), the parent initiated the transaction and generated the unrealized profit. Under ASC 810, 100% of the unrealized intercompany profit is eliminated against the parent''s controlling interest. NCI is unaffected because the subsidiary was the buyer, not the seller.
Wrong (A): Noncontrolling interest bears the elimination only in upstream sales where the subsidiary originated the profit, not in downstream sales.
Wrong (B): Pro rata allocation applies to upstream sales; downstream sale eliminations are charged entirely to the parent as the originating seller.
Wrong (D): The elimination affects both cost of goods sold and ending inventory on the consolidated balance sheet, not cost of goods sold alone.$EXPL$
WHERE id = 3180;

-- Q3181: Advanced Consolidations [medium/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): Under ASC 350, goodwill from a business combination is assigned to the reporting unit or units expected to benefit from the combination''s synergies. Goodwill impairment testing is subsequently performed at the reporting unit level, not at the entity or individual asset level.
Wrong (A): Goodwill is not tested at the consolidated entity level; ASC 350 requires assignment and testing at the reporting unit level for more precise impairment measurement.
Wrong (C): Goodwill is not allocated to individual assets; it represents the excess of purchase price over net identifiable assets and is assigned to reporting units.
Wrong (D): Goodwill is not recorded in retained earnings; it is a separately recognized intangible asset on the consolidated balance sheet.$EXPL$
