-- Q3186: Advanced Consolidations [hard/L2]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (A): Under ASC 805 using the full goodwill method, the fair value of NCI at the acquisition date is added to the parent''s purchase price to determine total fair value of the acquired entity. Total goodwill equals total fair value minus the fair value of net identifiable assets, attributing goodwill to both the parent and NCI.
Wrong (B): The parent''s acquisition cost is already known ($12 million); the NCI fair value is not needed to determine what the parent paid.
Wrong (C): NCI fair value has no bearing on dividend policy, which is a management decision unrelated to purchase price allocation.
Wrong (D): The parent''s investment account is measured by the consideration it transferred, not by the fair value of the noncontrolling interest.$EXPL$
