-- Q3189: Derivatives and Hedging [easy/L1]
-- Issues: #3
UPDATE questions SET
  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (B): A forward contract is a customized over-the-counter agreement between two parties to buy or sell an asset at a specified price on a specified future date. Under ASC 815-10-15-83, it qualifies as a derivative but is privately negotiated, introducing counterparty risk absent in exchange-traded instruments.
Wrong (A): This describes a futures contract, which is standardized and exchange-traded with daily margin settlement, unlike a customized forward.
Wrong (C): An option grants the right but not the obligation to transact; a forward contract obligates both parties to complete the transaction.
Wrong (D): A swap involves exchanging cash flows over multiple periods; a forward involves a single future exchange of an asset for a specified price.$EXPL$
